<title>USA: PepsiCo leaps at start of NYSE trade.</title>
<headline>PepsiCo leaps at start of NYSE trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>PepsiCo Inc shares opened New York Stock Exchange trade after an order-imbalance delay with a 3-7/8 gain to 35-3/4.</p>
<p>Subsequent minutes of intense NYSE trade quickly made PepsiCo shares the market's most active issue.</p>
<p>By 1020 EST, more than seven million shares changed hands as the initial price jump eased to 3-3/8.</p>
<p>The stocks's average daily volume is about four million shares.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1734)).</p>
